# Keep the build context small and never bake secrets or history into an image.
.git
.gitignore
.env
.env.example
deploy/
docs/
AGENTS.md
GLOSSARY.md
# The SQLite file, its sidecars, and any copy of it. `*.sqlite` alone misses
# `bookmarks.sqlite.bak`, the dated name the backup recipe in deploy/README.md
# suggests, and the -wal/-shm sidecars — and a -wal holds committed pages not
# yet in the database file. These must never reach an image layer or a remote
# builder.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite.*

# The default bind mount from docker-compose.yml, which holds the same file.
/data/

# CI configuration: the image does not need it, and leaving it in means every
# workflow edit invalidates the `COPY . .` layer and forces a full rebuild.
.github/
